   "source": [
    "### Measures of Central Tendency\n",
    "#### What are Measures of Central Tendency?\n",
    "Measures of Central Tendency are statistical measures that represent the center or typical value of a dataset. They summarize a large amount of data into a single representative value.\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Why are they important?\n",
    "Summarize large datasets.\n",
    "Compare different datasets.\n",
    "Identify the typical value.\n",
    "Used in Business Analytics, Finance, Healthcare, and AI/ML.\n",
    "#### The most common measures are:\n",
    "* Mean\n",
    "* Median\n",
    "* Mode\n",
    "* Weighted Mean\n",
    "* Geometric Mean\n",
    "* Harmonic Mean"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "3fe63a29-acdd-4997-af2e-4aec2930ee2e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Mean\n",
    "\n",
    "Mean is the average of all values in a dataset.\n",
    "It is calculated by adding all values and dividing by the number of values.\n",
    "\n",
    "Formula\n",
    "$$ Mean = \\frac{\\sum x}{n} $$\n",
    "\n",
    "Where:\n",
    "\n",
    "\\(x\\) = each value\n",
    "\\(n\\) = number of values"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 15,
   "id": "c84b3771-7ce3-4eed-a9fe-ffade697aee1",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "80.0\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "#Suppose the marks of 5 students are:\n",
    "\n",
    "#60, 70, 80, 90, 100\n",
    "Mean = (60+70+80+90+100) / 5\n",
    "print(Mean)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 17,
   "id": "1e2b3e1d-1d82-46f2-9d9e-9be645890b22",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "80.0\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "marks = [60, 70, 80, 90, 100]\n",
    "print(np.mean(marks))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "3d0178e0-6c30-43d3-90e2-98f556f4a0fa",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Median\n",
    "\n",
    "Median is the middle value when the data is arranged in ascending or descending order.\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Formula\n",
    "\n",
    "For an odd number of observations:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$ Median = \\text{Middle value} $$\n",
    "\n",
    "For an even number:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$ Median = \\frac{\\text{Two middle values}}{2} $$\n",
    "Numerical Example — Odd\n",
    "10, 20, 30, 40, 50\n",
    "\n",
    "Middle value:\n",
    "\n",
    "30\n",
    "\n",
    "Numerical Example — Even\n",
    "10, 20, 30, 40\n",
    "\n",
    "Two middle values:\n",
    "\n",
    "20 and 30"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 21,
   "id": "e4c1c1fa-12c6-42af-b044-bb718e97d0b6",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "20.0\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "\n",
    "numbers = [12, 18, 20, 25, 30]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(np.median(numbers))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 23,
   "id": "e6e1b56a-df9e-4dca-9cbf-b39de2a3a290",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Median: 30\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "import statistics\n",
    "\n",
    "data = [10, 20, 30, 40, 50]\n",
    "\n",
    "median = statistics.median(data)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Median:\", median)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "57aba6c6-541b-4835-ac96-00e43600a896",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Mode\n",
    "Mode is the value that occurs most frequently in a dataset.\n",
    "\n",
    "A dataset can have:\n",
    "\n",
    "* One mode → Unimodal\n",
    "* Two modes → Bimodal\n",
    "* Multiple modes → Multimodal\n",
    "* No mode → if every value occurs equally often"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ce0da77e-ab56-451b-9a32-8eeb35f40dd2",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Cat, Dog, Dog, Cat, Dog, Dog\n",
    "\n",
    "Mode:\n",
    "\n",
    "Dog"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 31,
   "id": "83a998dc-d333-4ce4-b985-5e448da46933",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "0    20\n",
      "dtype: int64\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "\n",
    "data = pd.Series([10, 20, 20, 30, 40, 20, 50])\n",
    "\n",
    "print(data.mode())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ec708008-aa41-4f95-8634-6da67f166818",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Weighted Mean\n",
    "\n",
    "Weighted Mean is an average where different values have different levels of importance or weights.\n",
    "\n",
    "Instead of treating every observation equally, we give some observations more importance.\n",
    "\n",
    "Formula\n",
    "$$ Weighted\\ Mean = \\frac{\\sum wx}{\\sum w} $$\n",
    "\n",
    "Where:\n",
    "\n",
    "\\(x\\) = value\n",
    "\\(w\\) = weight\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "1b460be4-4091-4295-8e69-50baf6d94acd",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "| Subject | Mark | Weight |\n",
    "| ------- | ---: | -----: |\n",
    "| Maths   |   80 |      3 |\n",
    "| Python  |   90 |      4 |\n",
    "| SQL     |   70 |      2 |\n",
    "\n",
    "Calculate:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$ Weighted\\ Mean = \\frac{80(3)+90(4)+70(2)} {3+4+2} $$ $$ =\\frac{240+360+140}{9} $$ $$ =\\frac{740}{9}=82.22 $$\n",
    "\n",
    "Weighted Mean = 82.22"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 37,
   "id": "c0722fd2-498c-43ce-b4c8-13aa7396a2c2",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Weighted Mean: 82.22222222222223\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "marks = [80, 90, 70]\n",
    "weights = [3, 4, 2]\n",
    "\n",
    "weighted_mean = sum(\n",
    "    mark * weight\n",
    "    for mark, weight in zip(marks, weights)\n",
    ") / sum(weights)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Weighted Mean:\", weighted_mean)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 39,
   "id": "fd010c96-0a2e-43b0-8ff4-34c66e7b460b",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "82.22222222222223\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "\n",
    "marks = [80, 90, 70]\n",
    "weights = [3, 4, 2]\n",
    "\n",
    "result = np.average(marks, weights=weights)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(result)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "38a42e85-dd99-4bdd-8544-b43e8c71fe8f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Geometric Mean\n",
    "Definition\n",
    "\n",
    "Geometric Mean is the average calculated by multiplying all values and taking the nth root.\n",
    "\n",
    "It is especially useful for growth rates, ratios, percentages and multiplicative data.\n",
    "\n",
    "Formula\n",
    "\n",
    "For \\(n\\) values:\n",
    "GM=\n",
    "4×16\n",
    "\t​\n",
    "\n",
    "$$ =\\sqrt{64} $$\n",
    "=8\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 43,
   "id": "0943fa92-06cf-4324-a4aa-1d4d5c5b98aa",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Geometric Mean: 7.999999999999998\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from statistics import geometric_mean\n",
    "\n",
    "data = [4, 16]\n",
    "\n",
    "result = geometric_mean(data)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Geometric Mean:\", result)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 46,
   "id": "113ac21b-3223-4798-ba42-ede45e8e1af4",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "7.999999999999998\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from scipy.stats import gmean\n",
    "\n",
    "data = [4, 16]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(gmean(data))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "4d6dd5a2-1f86-4495-96ba-3da0901e4c4c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Key Point\n",
    "\n",
    "Use geometric mean when values are related through multiplication or compounding.\n",
    "\n",
    "Common applications:\n",
    "\n",
    "* Investment returns\n",
    "* Population growth\n",
    "* Revenue growth\n",
    "* Compound growth\n",
    "* Ratios\n",
    "* Index numbers"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b4f906cc-87a6-4bda-aa40-720301693acf",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### Harmonic Mean\n",
    "Harmonic Mean is an average that is particularly useful for rates and ratios, especially when the numerator is constant.\n",
    "\n",
    "Formula\n",
    "$$ HM = \\frac{n}{\\sum \\frac{1}{x}} $$\n",
    "\n",
    "For two values:\n",
    "\n",
    "HM=\n",
    "2ab/a+b\n",
    "\t​\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "1a716efb-66b2-4c8e-9e7b-3d3c01fdeb87",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Suppose a car travels:\n",
    "\n",
    "60 km/h\n",
    "\n",
    "for one part of a journey and:\n",
    "\n",
    "40 km/h\n",
    "\n",
    "for another equal-distance part.\n",
    "\n",
    "The harmonic mean is:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$ HM = \\frac{2(60)(40)}{60+40} $$ $$ HM = \\frac{4800}{100} $$ $$ HM = 48 $$\n",
    "\n",
    "Average speed = 48 km/h"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "de81160a-d70a-4ad0-ba07-41ff7f0aff9e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "from statistics import harmonic_mean\n",
    "\n",
    "speeds = [60, 40]\n",
    "\n",
    "result = harmonic_mean(speeds)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Harmonic Mean:\", result)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "91c8c028-e7a6-4243-9ce0-02fad47ff9a9",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### AI/ML Example — F1 Score\n",
    "\n",
    "One of the most important applications of harmonic mean in AI/ML is the F1-score.\n",
    "\n",
    "F1 combines:\n",
    "\n",
    "Precision\n",
    "Recall\n",
    "\n",
    "Formula:\n",
    "\n",
    "F1=\n",
    "2×Precision×Recall/\n",
    "Precision+Recall\n",
    "\n",
    "\t​\n"
   ]

The F1-score balances both metrics and is especially useful for imbalanced datasets.
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9dbef869-543b-4de8-bbb2-e138c36ea71d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Mean → Average\n",
    "\n",
    "\"What is the average?\"\n",
    "\n",
    "Median → Middle\n",
    "\n",
    "\"What is the middle value?\"\n",
    "\n",
    "Mode → Most\n",
    "\n",
    "\"Which value occurs most?\"\n",
    "\n",
    "Weighted Mean → Importance\n",
    "\n",
    "\"Which values should have more importance?\"\n",
    "\n",
    "Geometric Mean → Growth\n",
    "\n",
    "\"How does something grow or compound?\"\n",
    "\n",
    "Harmonic Mean → Rates\n",
    "\n",
    "\"What is the appropriate average for rates?\""
   ]
  }
